## 7. One-line summary

The original kernel reduces 32 lanes to 1 four times per block, so wide VLEN
mostly idles. Repack N weight rows into N lanes and the reduction becomes a
vertical add - that is where large LMUL and wide VLEN finally turn into speed
(2.09x in-model). What is left is a memory stall, and one prefetch line removes
most of it (3.22x total).
